{"type": "message", "id": "0fa3b01d", "parentId": "a3e2c0a3", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T06:18:03.122Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:36", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \": Arizona grade 8 math NAEP score 2022 271\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 1000,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"aff256efda279851\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT ARIZONA  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"aff256efda279851\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011AZ8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7f30e30478bd4eb7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: <strong>The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7f30e30478bd4eb7\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"77b0097f7e8f5b4c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: Mathematics Highlights 2022\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"77b0097f7e8f5b4c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fbc97f90873166ab\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLooking at state/jurisdiction performance for eighth-graders in public schools, average scores were lower in 51 states/jurisdictions and not significantly different in 2. This is the largest number of states/jurisdictions with score declines in grade 8 mathematics going back to 2003. Among the states/jurisdictions with score declines, 18 scored lower than the national average score for public school students in 2022; 16 had average scores that were not significantly different from the national public average; and 17 scored higher. Explore detailed state average score results in the NAEP Mathematics Report Card\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fbc97f90873166ab\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"568af84217c063f6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"568af84217c063f6\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"15d5df1ce298903d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTo compare average mathematics scores between states/jurisdictions and the nation (public), use the NAEP State Profiles Tool. ... In the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"15d5df1ce298903d\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1166afedce68fec3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT NATION  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1166afedce68fec3\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011NP8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3a9e73edb7818bcb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: <strong>The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from 0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3a9e73edb7818bcb